# Automorphic L-functions and local factors, Part II: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It records which headline
theorems can be stated against the pinned APIs. None of the following headlines is
statable at these pins. The missing carriers are substantial library constructions;
plain matrix identities and arbitrary complex functions do not replace them.

* Unitary Siegel Eisenstein continuation and functional equation (README §1.3): lacks normalized unitary induced representations and automorphic Eisenstein families.
* Unitary local functional equation and exact spherical normalization (README §§2.2–2.4): lacks admissible unitary-group representations, normalized induced section families, doubling intertwiners and their local factors.
* Unitary global doubling identity and Garrett pullback (README §§3.1–3.3): lacks cuspidal adelic unitary representations, Petersson realizations and Eisenstein kernels.
* Meromorphic completed unitary standard L-function (README §3.4): lacks the same automorphic carriers and ramified unitary local factors.
* Holomorphic injection, branching and nonzero highest-line projection (README §§4.3 and 4.5–4.7): lacks Harish–Chandra modules for U(a,b), holomorphic discrete series, compact types and branching maps. The coefficient-field Cauchy decomposition of README §4.4 is expressible on the pinned Weyl modules, but it is a classical input to these branching theorems rather than a headline, and it remains a README target.
* Critical archimedean doubling nonvanishing and normalized algebraicity (README §§4.8–4.10): lacks those holomorphic representation carriers, the critical induced-fiber comparison and rational projected-kernel integral.
* (k,c) model existence, uniqueness, support and root elimination (README §§5.1–5.2 and 5.4): lacks smooth/Casselman–Wallach GL representations, generalized Speh representations and generalized Whittaker functionals.
* Generalized local continuation, multiplicity one and functional equation (README §§6.1–6.6): lacks normalized induction on classical groups, (k,c) models, continuous equivariant Hom spaces and doubling local factors.
* Highly ramified local stability (README §6.10): lacks those representation carriers and the canonical nongeneric GL pair factors.
* Auxiliary GL pole domination and doubling pole attainment (README §§7.1–7.6): lacks generalized Speh matrix-coefficient integrals, their meromorphic families and Langlands data.
* Nonessentially self-dual Speh Eisenstein holomorphy (README §§8.1–8.5): lacks residual automorphic Speh data, Eisenstein continuation and cuspidal-support exponents.
* Generalized global unfolding, completed functional equation and strip bounds (README §§9.1–9.3, and for SO₂ and GSpin₂, whose doubling period diverges, the split-torus branch of §§6.11 and 9.5): lacks cuspidal adelic classical-group representations, doubling Eisenstein kernels and completed local/global factors.
* Highly ramified global entireness (README §9.4, with the split-torus entireness criterion of §9.5): lacks those automorphic and completed-factor carriers.
* Twisted outside-S converse theorem (README §10.3): lacks admissible adelic GL representations, automorphy and all-rank Rankin–Selberg completions.
* Nongeneric cuspidal weak standard transfer (README §10.4): lacks cuspidal classical-group and automorphic GL representations, Satake parameters and archimedean standard transfer.
* All-place coarse compatibility and local transfer existence (README §§10.5–10.6): lacks those local/global representation carriers, supercuspidal support and gamma tests.
* Weak transfer for every irreducible automorphic representation (README §10.7): lacks general automorphic cuspidal-support realizations and GL isobaric induction.

The native algebraic representation, matrix, additive-character and measure carriers
do not include these admissibility, automorphy and globalization constructions.
No headline is represented by an unconstrained predicate or an admitted data object.
-/

